        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_978012005.1",
        "comments": "The assembly mPhyCat2.hap1.1 is based on 52x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny based on Physeter catodon (sperm whale) GCA_002837175.5. The chromosomes were named and oriented based on the reference Physeter catodon assembly GCA_002837175.5.The sex chromosomes were identified by read coverage and copy number in the haploid assembly. The exact order and orientation of the contigs in the centromers of chromosome 4 (66.3-73.7Mbp), chromsome 8 (40.0-53.7Mbp), chromosome 11 (135.4-149.9Mbp), chromosome 1 (37.7-41.9Mbp), chromosome 7 (55.6-60.5Mbp), chromosome 20 (38.1-54.6Mbp), chromosome 16 (61.5-68.3Mbp), chromosome 5 (81.5-88.6Mbp), chromosome 12 (67.1-81.7Mbp), chromosome 14 (31.8-36.3Mbp) and chromosome 17 (23.0-35.2Mbp) is unknown. A chromosome fusion of the reference chromosome 3 and 4 was observed. The new chromosome 3 originates from a fission of the reference chromosome 14.",
